`ActionComponent` includes 'action:menu' and 'action:group', but this loop forwards a single `ActionSchema` into whatever renderer is selected. `action:menu`/`action:group` renderers expect schemas with an `actions` array, so any action that sets `component: 'action:menu'` or `component: 'action:group'` will render nothing. Either constrain `component` here to the renderers that accept single actions (button/icon), or add an adapter that converts an ActionSchema into the correct menu/group schema shape.
```suggestion
          const requestedComponent: ActionComponent = action.component || 'action:button';
          // Inline actions must be single-action renderers; normalize menu/group to a button.
          const componentType: ActionComponent =
            requestedComponent === 'action:menu' || requestedComponent === 'action:group'
              ? 'action:button'
              : requestedComponent;
```

This pre-filter drops actions that have no `locations` field. Since `action:bar` treats missing/empty `locations` as “show anywhere”, record header actions without explicit locations won’t render. Consider passing `objectDef.actions` directly to the ActionBar (it already filters by `location`), or include actions with missing/empty `locations` in this filter.
```suggestion
  // Include actions that:
  // - have no locations (treated as "show anywhere"),
  // - have an empty locations array,
  // - or explicitly include "record_header".
  const recordHeaderActions = (objectDef.actions || []).filter((a: any) => {
    const locations = a.locations;
    if (!locations || locations.length === 0) {
      return true;
    }
    return locations.includes('record_header');
  });
```
